	(text "Tuning structures (bottom side, 0402 jumper positions, copper geometry identical to the demo board):\nTUNE1 (698-960 MHz): antenna pin 4 -> via -> pad 6 ... pad 1.  Gaps 6-5 (R5), 5-4 (R6), 4-3 (R7) are bridged by copper; gaps 3-2 (R8) and 2-1 (R9) are open.\nTUNE2 (1710-3800 MHz): antenna pin 5 -> via -> pad A -> B -> D -> C -> E.  A-B (R1) and B-C are bridged by copper; R2, R3, R4 gaps are open.\nShift resonance LOWER: fit 0R 0402 across open gaps (R1..R9).  Shift HIGHER: cut the bridge traces.  Pins 3/4/9/10 share one copper area, pin 6/7 are unused dummies (as on the demo board)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 34.544 158.242 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "524c4177-451e-546a-aecc-5c9ed03483bb")
	)
	(text "KYOCERA AVX P822601 broadband LTE/LPWA antenna - pi matching network and tuning structures\nLayout copied from the P822601-01 demo board (datasheet TDS-ANT-0053 rev 3, pages 10, 12, 13)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "afcdf30d-d63d-5e91-bd82-bc6d0ee3d75b")
	)
	(text "FEEDLINE SIMULATION (openEMS via gerber2ems, see electronics/sim/feedline, 2026-10-18). Stack JLC05161H-1080, reference plane\n   GND1 (In1.Cu), 76 um prepreg, er 3.91.\n1. The 0.158 mm microstrip nRF9151 ANT -> matching input is 49 ohm as drawn: |S11| < -35 dB and < 0.01 dB loss from 0.65 to 4\n   GHz without J11. Keep 0.158 mm; a 0.135 mm trace is worse.\n2. J11 U.FL pad 1 (1.05 x 1.0 mm) on 76 um of prepreg is a 0.48 pF shunt on the feed: line |S11| drops to -16 dB (B1/B2/B3), -14\n   dB (B7), -11 dB (n78), costing up to 4 dB of return loss at the modem in the high bands (n78 -9 -> -6.5 dB with the demo-\n   board matching). FIX: void in GND1 under J11 pad 1, pad + 0.25 mm = 1.55 x 1.5 mm (board x 195.725-197.275, y\n   130.225-131.725): line |S11| < -22 dB everywhere, 51-57 ohm, no loss. A 0.5 mm margin overshoots (62 ohm at 3.5 GHz); cutting\n   GND2 too changes nothing. Keep GND2 and the via fence. Alternative: Murata MM8130-2600 switch connector (footprint already in\n   Components.pretty) instead of a tapped U.FL, or no J11 at all.\n3. Matching: the measured bare antenna (sparam/Ant_P822601) with the p.12 values does not reproduce the measured demo board\n   (sparam/EVB_P822601-01); the demo board behaves like ~22 nH / 2.4 pF / 3.3 nH / no P4, closest to the Appendix 1 set (24 nH /\n   2.4 pF / 4.7 nH / DNI). Expect to retune L5/C5/L6/C8 on the real board with a VNA at J11; keep the DNI pads.\n4. Not simulated: the antenna itself and the pi-network pads (lumped parts). Ask JLCPCB for impedance control on net /RF_ANT (50\n   ohm, 0.158 mm over L2) if their er differs from 3.91.\n5. MATCHING NETWORK in the EM model (sim/feedline pi_neck / pi_void_neck, 8-port openEMS + measured bare antenna, ideal L/C, worst\n   |S11| at the modem): datasheet p.12 values 24n/2.4p/1n/0.3p give only -3.4 dB in B3 and -3.5 dB in B7 on this board. With the\n   J11 GND1 void the best single set is L5 22 nH, C5 3.6 pF, L6 2.2 nH, C8 0.5 pF (or 20n/3.3p/2.4n/0.4p): -9 dB or better in\n   B28 to n78. The void is worth 2-4 dB in B3/B7 with the network fitted. Values are a starting point: real 0402 inductor SRF and\n   this board's ground plane shift them, tune with a VNA at J11."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 172.72 100.33 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.9 0.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b621c11b-2e2d-5b6f-b7e4-1d0a5a68d1cd")
	)
	(text "Default matching (datasheet p.12, 140x50 mm demo board), datasheet position = designator:  P1 = L5 = 24nH   S1 = C5 = 2.4pF   P2 = C6 = DNI   P3 = C7 = DNI   S2 = L6 = 1.0nH   P4 = C8 = 0.3pF   R1-R9 = DNI\nAppendix 1 broadband option (4G/5G + NTN L/S band): L6 (S2) = 4.7nH, C8 (P4) = DNI.  All parts 0402. The L5/C5/C6/C7/L6/C8 pads sit inline with the antenna feed trace on the top side next to pin 1."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 40.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c4989759-7973-548b-afd7-dd11cdcf7a55")
	)
